    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for June 11th is anchored by the elite offensive profile of **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 76.60 score makes him the clear must-start today. Despite facing a formidable arm in Woo, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable right-handed platoon advantage that elevates his floor significantly. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (68.81) and **Josh Jung** (67.70) represent our most reliable assets; **Josh Jung** is particularly intriguing as his BvP history against Wacha (28 PA) and favorable wind conditions out of the park provide a meaningful hedge against a middle-of-the-road matchup. While **Andy Pages** (64.76) holds a strong position in the two-hole, the team is counting on him to capitalize on the high-volume opportunities created by the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision involved the lower-third utility spots, where **Sam Antonacci** (41.83) and **Coby Mayo** (42.53) are both flirting with the \"below floor\" threshold. **Sam Antonacci** suffers from a significant L/L platoon disadvantage against Perez and a bottom-of-the-order penalty, while **Coby Mayo** is hampered by a challenging matchup against Woo. Despite the low scores, these two remain active to preserve our game caps, as our primary bench options\u2014including **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg**\u2014are unavailable due to either scheduling off-days or IL designations. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Liam Hicks** (59.92) closely; while his lead-off spot against Kelly provides a substantial +10% order boost, his reliance on recency bias and situational platoon edges makes him a high-variance play. We have been forced to bench the remainder of our depth\u2014including **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Wade Meckler**\u2014to maintain roster flexibility. The primary risk today is the SP skill of Woo, which could suppress the offensive output of both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** if they fail to leverage their park advantages early in the count.",
